{"slug":"phaseolus-vulgaris","plant":{"taxon":"Phaseolus vulgaris","family":"Fabaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":5350452,"wikidata":"Q42339","iucn":"LC","gbif_occurrences":289305,"common_name":"French bean","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"French Beans","monograph_id":"cul:029-french-beans","confidence":"high","note":"Kidney/French bean; standard identification."}],"n_compounds":663,"top_compounds":[{"name":"benzene","qid":"Q2270"},{"name":"adenine","qid":"Q15277"},{"name":"toluene","qid":"Q15779"},{"name":"vanillin","qid":"Q33495"},{"name":"urea","qid":"Q48318"},{"name":"xanthine","qid":"Q50980"},{"name":"benzyl alcohol","qid":"Q52353"},{"name":"1-hexanol","qid":"Q76933"}],"epmc_total":11639,"trials":41,"claims":[{"concept_id":"kidney_disease","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":11,"lift":0.1,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"asthma_dyspnea","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":0.02,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"constipation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":0.12,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"diuresis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":2,"lift":0.14,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"dyspepsia","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.02,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"sexual_function","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.03,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"urolithiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":2,"lift":0.27,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:029-french-beans":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: French Beans","headword":"French Beans","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"These also belong to Dame Venus, and being dried and beat to powder, are as great strengtheners of the kidneys as any are; neither is there a better remedy than it; a dram at a time taken in white wine to prevent the stone, or to cleanse the kidneys of gravel or stoppage. The ordinary French Beans are of an easy digestion; they move the belly, provoke urine, enlarge the breast that is straightened with shortness of breath, engender sperm, and incite to venery. And the scarlet coloured Beans, in regard of the glorious beauty of their colour, being set near a quickset hedge, will much adorn the same, by climbing up thereon, so that they may be discerned a great way, not without admiration of the beholders at a distance. But they will go near to kill the quicksets by cloathing them in scarlet.","spans":[{"start":103,"end":110,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":217,"end":222,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":242,"end":249,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":253,"end":259,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":314,"end":323,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":330,"end":344,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":346,"end":359,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"action"},{"start":406,"end":425,"concept_id":"asthma_dyspnea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":427,"end":441,"concept_id":"sexual_function","polarity":"action"},{"start":457,"end":463,"concept_id":"sexual_function","polarity":"action"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:029-french-beans":{"103":"kidneys","217":"the stone (urinary calculus)","242":"kidneys","253":"gravel: small urinary concretions","314":"digestion / indigestion","330":"purges / opens / loosens the belly: laxative, purgative","346":"provokes urine: diuretic","406":"shortness of breath: dyspnoea","427":"increases sperm / breeds seed","457":"provokes / stirs up / abates venery, bodily lust"}},"images":[]}